      "file": "thrust_bearing_assembly_pressure.glb",
      "title": "Oil-film pressure builds toward the trailing edge",
      "description": "Each pad tilts freely on its pivot so a converging oil wedge forms between the rotating collar and the pad face. Oil dragged into the narrowing gap builds hydrodynamic pressure, highest toward the trailing edge, which carries the axial thrust without metal contact (film typically ≈ 10–50 µm). Pad temperature (RTD in the babbitt) is the main health indicator; the inactive pads take reverse thrust during start-up or surge.",
